import lib/filesystem.dl

create a temporary directory and set first to it
create a temporary directory and set second to it
print whether first succeeded as a line
print whether second succeeded as a line
print whether (first's directory path is not second's directory path) as a line

set origin to the file system entry at first's directory path
set counterpart to the file system entry at second's directory path
print whether ((origin lookup succeeded) and (origin was found)) and (origin is a directory) as a line
print whether ((counterpart lookup succeeded) and (counterpart was found)) and (counterpart is a directory) as a line

set file to first's directory path + the string form of "/payload.bin"
set payload to a new string buffer containing 5 bytes
store 65 as a byte into the data of payload at 0
store 0 as a byte into the data of payload at 1
store 66 as a byte into the data of payload at 2
store 67 as a byte into the data of payload at 3
store 68 as a byte into the data of payload at 4
write payload to the file at file and print whether it succeeded as a line

open the file at file for streaming reads
set input to it
print whether input succeeded as a line
read up to 3 bytes from input and set initial to it
print whether initial succeeded as a line
print initial's count as a line
print whether initial reached the end of file as a line
print (the character at 0 in initial's data) as a line
print (the character at 1 in initial's data) as a line
print (the character at 2 in initial's data) as a line

read up to 3 bytes from input and set following to it
print whether following succeeded as a line
print following's count as a line
print whether following reached the end of file as a line
print (the character at 0 in following's data) as a line
print (the character at 1 in following's data) as a line

read up to 3 bytes from input and set final to it
print whether final succeeded as a line
print final's count as a line
print whether final reached the end of file as a line

read up to (-1) bytes from input and set invalid to it
print whether invalid succeeded as a line
print invalid's count as a line
print whether invalid reached the end of file as a line
print whether (the length of invalid's error message) > 0 as a line

open the file at "tests/required/filesystem_streaming_temp/missing.bin" for streaming reads
set missing to it
print whether missing succeeded as a line
print whether the length of missing's error message > 0 as a line

remove the filesystem tree at first's directory path and set purge to it
remove the filesystem tree at second's directory path and set removal to it
print whether purge succeeded as a line
print whether removal succeeded as a line
